The decline of the nation-state is really a decline of the specifically national content of the state and an opportunity to[ create a cos]mopolitan state system[ that] is better able to deal with the problems that all nations face in the world today. Economic globalisation, trans[national] terrorism, global warming: the litany is familiar and daunting.[ There] are a host of problems that are clearly beyond the power of the old order of nation-states to cope with. The answer to global problems that are gathering ominously[ all around] and that refuse to yield to nation-state solutions[ is for politics] to[ take a] quantum leap from the nation-state system[ to] the cosmopolitan state system. Politics[ needs] to[ regain] credibility in order to craft real solutions.
